            <ArticleTitle>Transcatheter repair of a large coronary pseudoaneurysm using ultrasound guidance and vein-covered stents.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>701-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case-report describes a large pseudoaneurysm of the proximal left anterior descending coronary artery, fissured in the pericardium, developed 4 days after rotational and directional atherectomy followed by stent implantation. A successful percutaneous repair was obtained with 2 vein-covered stents implanted and expanded under ultrasound guidance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
